# The v2 shell is unlaunched. Disallowing the base covers every page under it,
# including mounts that do not exist yet — per-page <meta name="robots"> was
# already inconsistent (HomeMarketDetailPage had none), and every new mount is
# a fresh chance to forget one.
#
# Shell pages duplicate public content (/dashboard-v2/skills vs /skills,
# /dashboard-v2/markets/:id vs /:id). Those public URLs are prerendered and
# carry the ClawHub inbound links; a crawlable duplicate can only compete with
# them.
#
# DELETE THIS RULE AT THE ROUTING FLIP, when the shell takes over /dashboard
# and stops being a duplicate.
User-agent: *
Disallow: /dashboard-v2
